      "heading": "Paper 9700/42: Key messages",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "heading": null,
          "bullets": [
            "In questions requiring comparisons to be made such as <b>4(d)</b>, similarities and differences must be made clear with statements that address one feature at a time and indicate how this feature is the same or different for the two (or more) things being compared. One way to do this is to construct a table with each row considering one feature only. The same principle applies in questions requiring differences to be identified, such as <b>8(c)</b>.",
            "Candidates are often expected to quote data relating to graphs or table. When quoting data, it is essential that appropriate units are used."
          ]
        }
      ]
